    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d137">

                <pb facs="0290" n="186" sameAs="frus:frus1890/pg186"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Blaine to Mr.
                            Denby</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1890-05-17"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 17,
                        1890</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 530.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your No. 1068 of the 18th of
                    March last, I transmit a copy of a letter from the Secretary of the Treasury
                    concurring in the view that the certificate of the taotai, properly viséed by
                    the minister or consul of the United States, would be sufficient to authorize
                    the collector of customs at the United States port where Mr. Howe, the Chinese
                    subject whose case you present, arrives to permit his landing.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">James G. Blaine.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d137-a1.xml" xpointer="d137-a1"/>
            </div>
